    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0531" n="413" xml:id="pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Detention/67</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Good</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-04">May 4, 1929</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">WPD 3297–32</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With reference to your
                    letter of May 1, 1929 (Me 812.00 Detention/60 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >62</hi>]), in which you request that the United States Army authorities
                    continue to hold in custody the eighteen armed Mexican rebels who recently
                    crossed the border at Sasabe, Arizona, I am pleased to advise you that this will
                    be done and that they will not be turned over to the United States Immigration
                    authorities without prior consultation with your Department.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James W. Good</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
